  "notes": "{萎|しぼ}む describes something losing its fullness — flowers wilting, balloons deflating, or spirits fading.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {萎|しぼ}ませる (transitive, causative)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{萎|しぼ}んでいる describes the resulting state: the flower has already wilted, the balloon is already flat.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {花|はな}が{萎|しぼ}む: flowers wilt\n- {風船|ふうせん}が{萎|しぼ}む: a balloon deflates\n- {気持|きも}ちが{萎|しぼ}む: spirits sink\n- やる{気|き}が{萎|しぼ}む: motivation fades\n- {期待|きたい}が{萎|しぼ}む: expectations fade\n\nOPPOSITE:\n- {膨|ふく}らむ: to swell, to inflate, to expand",
